# UI style guidelines

Source of truth for tokens: `@theme` in `src/renderer/src/assets/index.css`.
Shared recipes: `src/renderer/src/ui/classes.js`. Compose with `cn()` from `src/renderer/src/ui/cn.js`
(it knows the custom shadow tokens, so `cn(card, 'shadow-none')` merges correctly).

Style UI with Tailwind utilities. Do not add component CSS files or plain CSS rules.
Do not re-declare a recipe locally (dialog shell, menu item, popover, search input…): import it.

## Direction

Calm, neutral canvas; white surfaces; one coral accent per region; teal for progress/done.
Hierarchy comes from type size and spacing, not from heavy weights, thick borders or colored washes.

## Page structure

- Every top-level view renders `<AppHeader active="…" onNavigate={…}>` (brand, nav, `center`, `actions`,
  optional toolbar `children`). The active nav tab is the page title; do not add a visible page `<h1>`.
- Page root: `pageShell`. Pop-out/embedded views use `AppHeader` without `active` and pass `title`/`subtitle`.

## Tokens (use these — do not invent parallel palettes or hex values)

- **Ink:** `text-ink` (primary), `text-ink-soft` (secondary/meta), `text-ink-faint` (placeholders, tertiary)
- **Surfaces:** `bg-surface` (cards/panels), `bg-cream` (subtle fill: sidebars, footers, wells), `bg-cream-deep` (page canvas)
- **Accent:** `bg-coral` / `text-coral-deep` / `bg-coral-soft` (primary actions, selection, “in progress”)
- **Secondary:** `bg-teal` / `text-teal` / `bg-teal-tint` (progress, done)
- **Semantic tints:** `chip-programs-*` (programs), `chip-status-*` (done/new), `chip-theme-*` (themes), `warn*` (notices), `danger*` (destructive)
- **Type scale:** `text-2xs` 11 · `text-xs` 12 · `text-sm` 13 · `text-base` 14 (body) · `text-md` 15 · `text-lg` 17 · `text-xl` 20 · `text-2xl` 24 · `text-3xl` 30. No `text-[…rem]`.
- **Weights:** `font-medium` UI, `font-semibold` labels/buttons/card titles, `font-bold` display headings only. No `font-black` / `font-extrabold`.
- **Fonts:** `font-display` (Bricolage Grotesque) for headings and card titles, `font-body` (Geist) for everything else.
- **Radii:** `rounded-sm` (8) controls · `rounded-md` (12) content cards, menus · `rounded-lg` (16) large cards, dialogs, columns · `rounded-full` pills (chips, badges, filter pills) only. No `rounded-[Npx]` above 4px.
- **Shadows:** `shadow-card` resting · `shadow-lift` hover · `shadow-panel` popovers/dialogs · `shadow-focus` input focus · `shadow-ring` / `shadow-ring-soft` selection
- **Hairlines:** `border-ink/8` (surfaces) · `border-ink/12` (controls) · `border-ink/20` (hover)
- **Motion:** `ease-pop` (crisp ease-out, no overshoot), `duration-150`

## Buttons

- `btnPrimary` — one per region. `btnGhost` — secondary. `btnQuiet` — tertiary/toolbar. `btnDanger` — destructive.
- `btnCompact` modifier for dense rows and card footers. `btnOn` for pressed toggles (with `aria-pressed`).
- Icon-only: `iconOnly` + a Lucide icon + `aria-label` + `title`.
- Buttons are `rounded-sm`, not pills.

## Content cards

- `card` / `cardLg` (+ `cardHover` when clickable). Title in `font-display font-semibold`, meta in `text-ink-soft`.
- Secondary actions on media cards appear on hover/focus (`opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 group-focus-within:opacity-100`).
- Status: small badge (`badgeAccent`, `badgeSuccess`, `badgeTheme`, `badgeWarn`) or a colored dot — never a full colored border or wash.

## Fields

- Inputs `fieldControl`, selects `selectControl`, search `searchInput` + `<Search className={searchIcon} />`.
- Labels `fieldLabel` (sentence case). Use `eyebrow` only for small uppercase group kickers.

## Overlays

- Dialogs: `dialogShell` + a `max-w-*`, `dialogBody`, `dialogTitle`, `dialogLead`. Backdrop and open animation are global.
- Menus: `popover` container, `menuItem` rows (`<span>` title + `<small>` hint), `menuDivider`.
- Notices/banners: `notice` with a leading Lucide icon and compact buttons.
- Segmented choices: `segmented` + `segmentedItem` with `aria-pressed`.

## Icons

Use `lucide-react`. Size with Tailwind (`size-4`). Never use text glyphs (`‹ › ○ ▶ ···`) or emoji as UI chrome.
